
## Development Commands

```bash
# Test
npm test

# Lint
npm run lint

# Build
npm run build
```

## Hephaestus Commands

Shared commands from the [hephaestus](https://github.com/amurshak/hephaestus) submodule:

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `/autopilot` | Full pipeline — pick issue, plan, implement, test, ship, finish |
| `/start-issue 42` | Plan-critique-implement for one issue |
| `/ship` | Code review → quality gates → CHANGELOG → PR → auto-merge |
| `/finish` | Close issue, clean branches, file follow-ups |
| `/refactor` | Autonomous refactoring with review gate |
| `/research` | Parallel web research with synthesized findings |
| `/critique` | Adversarial review — code or strategy |
| `/create-issue` | Codebase-informed issue creation with labels |
| `/test-issue` | Run quality gates, verify acceptance criteria |
| `/update-docs` | Sync CLAUDE.md, CHANGELOG with recent work |
| `/orient` | Cold-start: repo state, open issues, next action |

## Agents

| Agent | Role |
|---|---|
| **coder** | Writes code in isolated worktrees. Parallel for independent tasks. |
| **reviewer** | Security, architecture, test adequacy. PASS / PASS WITH CHANGES / FAIL. |
| **tester** | Runs test/lint/build from Development Commands above. |
| **explorer** | Read-only codebase investigation. |
| **researcher** | Web search with source cross-referencing. |

## Updating Hephaestus

```bash
.hephaestus/update.sh
```

This pulls the latest and re-runs install.sh to pick up new commands and agents.
